dressbook><name>ASHIZAWA, SUSUMU</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>THE YOKOHAMA RUBBER CO., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>UDAGAWA, YOSHITAKA</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ASHIZAWA SUSUMU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>UDAGAWA YOSHITAKA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ASHIZAWA, SUSUMU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>UDAGAWA, YOSHITAKA</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A method of separating a vulcanized or unvulcanized rubber into a rubber ingredient and a filler ingredient such as carbon black which comprises liquefying the vulcanized or unvulcanized rubber at ordinary temperature and ordinary pressure; and a method of separating from a rubber composite a component other than those. The methods comprise immersing, optionally with stirring, a rubber composite or a vulcanized rubber composition each in the form of a block in an organic solvent containing 0.01 to 50% peroxide such as benzoyl peroxide to liquefy the vulcanized rubber composition in the solvent and separating the filler ingredient and other components by centrifugal separation, membrane separation, or decantation.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Cette invention concerne un procédé de séparation du caoutchouc, vulcanisé ou non vulcanisé, en un ingrédient de caoutchouc et un ingrédient de charge tel que du noir de carbone. Ce procédé consiste à liquéfier le caoutchouc vulcanisé ou non vulcanisé à une température et sous une pression normales. L'invention concerne également un procédé permettant d'extraire d'un composite de caoutchouc un composant autre que ceux susmentionnés. Le procédé consiste en l'immersion, avec brassage éventuel, d'un bloc de caoutchouc composite ou d'une composition de caoutchouc vulcanisé dans un solvant organique renfermant de 0,01 % à 50 % de peroxyde tel que du peroxyde de benzoyle de manière à liquéfier la composition de caoutchouc vulcanisé dans le solvant et à séparer l'ingrédient de charge et autres éléments constitutifs par centrifugation, séparation membranaire ou décantation.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>